    "knowledge_point": "Identifying a Radial Line Given Its Polar Equation",
    "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve  $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}?$",
    "worked_solution": "The polar curve defined by the equation $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ is the ray that starts at the origin and makes a counterclockwise angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nThe correct answer is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980294/assets/f548b48d223ba5164e8e7335b67dc27dd89347bc368be0cc992c456fe5360b85.png)",
